What customers ask most about our Business Managers (BM). For warranty details, see [Warranty](/docs/questions-bank/warranty).

### What is a Business Manager (BM)?

Business Manager is Meta's official platform to manage advertising assets, Pages, ad accounts, and team collaboration safely and professionally.

### What is the difference between Verified BM and Unverified BM?

1. **Verified BM:** Has completed Meta's verification process. Higher trust, better stability, higher limits, and lower risk.
2. **Unverified BM:** Not verified. Easier to get but lower trust and more restrictions.

### What types of Business Managers does GOADS provide?

We specialize in high-quality super aged and verified Business Managers:

1. BM5 Super Aged (Unlimited DSL)
2. BM10 Verified (Unlimited DSL)
3. BM50 and above, on request

{% callout variant="info" title="BM1, BM3 and the $250-limit BM5 are no longer sold" %}
Those tiers were worth buying for the **native ad accounts** inside them, and native accounts stopped being reliable on Meta. Every Business Manager we sell today is built to hold **agency ad accounts**, which we share in with full admin.
{% /callout %}

### What is BM5 Super Aged (Unlimited DSL)?

A super aged, verified Business Manager with no daily spending limit. It holds up to 5 ad accounts and carries real spending history, which is why it is our entry point rather than a step up.

### What is BM10 Verified (Unlimited DSL)?

A very strong and highly trusted Business Manager with no daily spending limit. It holds up to 10 ad accounts and carries a large spending history.

### Which BM should I choose for long-term stability?

BM5 Super Aged covers most advertisers, from solo buyers through scaling agencies. Move up to BM10 Verified or higher when you need more than five ad accounts in one place, or you are running several clients or geographies.

### How do ad accounts get into the BM?

We share **agency ad accounts** into your Business Manager. Send us your BM ID and the account appears inside it with full admin access.

{% callout variant="warning" title="Native ad accounts are a dead end" %}
You can still create a native ad account inside a BM, but Meta disables them quickly and they carry no warranty from us. Buy agency ad accounts instead: each one is covered until it has spent $1,000.
{% /callout %}

### Do you sell WhatsApp Business API (WABA) Business Managers?

Yes, on request. WABA messaging tiers are not listed in the catalog because availability and limits change, so message support for current options and pricing.

### What is the warranty on Business Managers?

7 days on the Business Manager itself. Agency ad accounts shared into it are covered separately, each until it has spent $1,000.

